# H signals — the reading-order vocabulary.
#
# FORMAT: one `reason: regex` per line. Blank lines and # comments ignored. A signal matches a
# path at its start, at a segment start, or after a word separator inside a filename.
#
# THIS IS A HINT, NOT A COMPLETENESS SIGNAL. Measured across five real repositories on 2026-08-02:
# 59% label precision, 20% of production files matched, and 0-of-6 recall on the files that
# actually produced findings. It guesses semantics from names the TARGET's authors chose, so it
# works when they happen to have used one of these words and not otherwise. A file no signal
# reaches is reported as UNREAD, never as clean — that is what makes the miss safe.
#
# IT LIVES HERE, NOT IN THE BINARY, SO IT CAN BE ITERATED FROM USAGE. Add a word after a sweep
# that missed something and reinstall the skill; no binary release is involved. Extend per-repo
# with a `.slop-h-signals` file in the target, same format.
#
# BEFORE ADDING A WORD: the tables are coupled to the tier split. Adding a term to a tier-1 group
# can move a file into the required tier. Measured: adding `ratelimit` to money/value matched
# ghola's internal/client/ratelimit.go, taking it from 10 required to 1 and deferring 9 files on a
# repo readable in one pass. Every test passed. Re-measure on real repos after any edit here.

